"""
ATLAS - Museum Helmet (Jetson + Claude + Vosk + RAG)
=====================================================
Full integrated system: Jetson Orin Nano hardware, Claude API for
generation, Vosk for streaming STT, ChromaDB-backed RAG for museum
artwork knowledge, YOLOE for vision, Piper for TTS.

Hardware:
  - Jetson Orin Nano (JetPack 6.1, CUDA 12.6)
  - Raspberry Pi Camera Module 3 (IMX708) via NVIDIA Argus / GStreamer
  - USB MillSO mic on sounddevice index 1 (hw:1,0)
  - USB speaker on plughw:0,0 (UACDemoV1.0)

Prerequisites:
  pip install chromadb sentence-transformers anthropic vosk \\
              sounddevice opencv-python numpy python-dotenv \\
              ultralytics
  The atlas/ package and data/artworks/ must exist
  (created by the day-2 RAG bootstrap).
  Set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in .env.

Multilanguage:
  - Three languages: English, French, Spanish.
  - Each language has its own Vosk model and Piper voice.
  - Voice commands switch between them.
  - Claude is told the active language and replies in it.
  - Ack WAVs are pre-rendered in all 3 languages at startup.

RAG integration:
  - Loaded once at startup, kept in memory.
  - For user questions: semantic search with score threshold.
    Above the threshold, the matching sheet is injected as
    ground truth into the Claude prompt.
  - For camera events: direct lookup by ID via YOLOE_TO_ARTWORK_ID
    mapping, so detection of "mona lisa painting" pulls the full
    Mona Lisa sheet immediately.
"""

